      "url": "https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/DivyaMascarenhas_07082026233427_JSWSLSEIntimationforChangeinSMPAugust72026.pdf",
      "text": "JSWSL: MUM: SEC: SE: 2026-27/08/03 August 7, 2026 1. National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Exchange Plaza, Plot No. C/1, G Block Bandra – Kurla Complex Bandra (E), Mumbai – 400 051 NSE Symbol: JSWSTEEL Kind Attn: Listing Department 2. BSE Limited Corporate Relationship Dept. Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers Dalal Street, Mumbai – 400 001. Scrip Code No.500228 Kind Attn: Listing Department Subject : Disclosure under Regulation 30 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 – Change in Senior Management Dear Sir/Madam, Pursuant to Regulation 30 read with Part A of Sc hedule III of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (‘Listing Regulations’), we hereby inform you that the Boar d of Directors, based on the reco mmendation of the Nomination & Remuneration Committee, considered and approved appointment of Mr. P P Varma, Executive Vice President & Plant Head - Dolvi, Salav & Anjar and Mr. S M Kumar, Sr. Vice President, Plant Head - Salem, as a part of Senior Management of the Company, effective August 7, 2026. Further, we hereby inform changes in senior mana gement of the Company effective August 7, 2026 as under: • Mr. Ashish Chandra, President-Dolvi, Sala v & Anjar Works has ceased to be Senior Management of the Company, consequent to his resignation from the services of the Company due to personal reasons and to pursue career opportunities outside JSW Group; and • Mr. B N S Prakash Rao has transitioned from the role of Senior Management of the Company as Plant Head - Salem Works, and has been appointed as Head – Centre of Excellence for Alloy Steel. Details required under Regulation 30 of the Listing Regulations read along with SEBI Master Circular No. HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFD-POD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026 are enclosed herewith as ‘Annexure A & B’. A copy of the letter of resignation of Mr. Ashish Chandra is enclosed herewith as Annexure C. The aforesaid disclosure is also available on the Company’s website at www.jsw.in. Thanking You, Yours faithfully, For JSW STEEL LIMITED Manoj Prasad Singh Company Secretary (in the interim capacity) Annexure A Details as required in accordance with SEBI Master Circular No. HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFDPOD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026 Sl. Details of events that need to be provided Appointment of Mr. P P Varma, Executive Vice President & Plant Head - Dolvi, Salav & Anjar, as a part of Senior Management of the Company Appointment of Mr. S M Kumar, Sr. Vice President, Plant Head - Salem, as a part of Senior Management of the Company 1. Reason for change Appointment Appointment 2. Date of Appointment & terms of appointment August 7, 2026. August 7, 2026. 3. Brief profile Mr. P P Varma has a dynamic career of 39 years, which reflects the diverse experience in Steel Plant operations. Mr. Varma joined JSW Steel on 31st May 2004 and since then has done key roles such as Head of Iron and Agglomeration Zone and the Chief Operating Officer for Dolvi Plant. He has played a pivotal role in shaping the growth of the Dolvi Plant and strengthening its manufacturing capabilities. Mr. Varma has been part of the coveted leadership program (Future Fit Leaders) at JSW Steel in 2017. Mr. Varma holds a degree in Bachelors of Technology (Mechanical) from IIT BHU (1987). Mr. S M Kumar has a dynamic career of 35 years, showing a strong experience in Steel Plant operations. Mr. Kumar joined JSW Steel on 1st June 2006 and since then has done diverse roles in Customer Services and Market Development, Quality Assurance, and Operations & Maintenance. Mr. Kumar has played a pivotal role in strengthening operational practices across the Salem Plant and has been a key contributor to the growth journey of the unit. Mr. Kumar has been part of the coveted leadership program (Future Fit Leaders) at JSW Steel in 2017. Mr. Kumar holds a degree in Bachelors of Technology (Metallurgy) from IIT Madras (1991). 4. Disclosure of relationships between Directors Not applicable Not applicable Annexure B Details as required in accordance with SEBI Master Circular No. HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFDPOD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026 Sl. Details of events that need to be provided Cessation of Mr. Ashish Chandra, President-Dolvi, Salav & Anjar Works as Senior Management of the Company Mr. B N S Prakash Rao has transitioned from the role of Senior Management of the Company as Plant Head - Salem Works, and has been appointed as Head – Centre of Excellence for Alloy Steel. 1. Reason for change Cessation Transition to new role 2. Date of Appointment & terms of appointment August 7, 2026. Please note that Mr. Chandra ceases to be part of Senior Management effective August 7, 2026, while he would be relieved from the services of the Company with effect from close of business hours on August 31, 2026 (last working day). August 7, 2026. 3. Brief profile Not applicable Not applicable 4. Disclosure of relationships between Directors Not applicable Not applicable",
